-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 8: SERVICE OUT OF SINGAPORE (Rules 1 to 8, including Rule 4A).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE: the text says yes on these facts.  JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words
-- (a flat negative, an "unless", an "if", "where", "when" or "upon" that is not met, a stated period that has run).
-- NOTHING: the text does not answer (a list not closed, a grant limited by its own wording, a scope limit with no "only",
-- a term or law outside the sources).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Order 3, Rule 2(1) is a caveat on every answer in these Rules and is not threaded as an input.
--
-- The foreign law, the Hague Service Convention, the Warsaw Convention and the State Immunity Act are outside these sources:
-- where a function needs what they say, it takes it as a plain yes/no input.

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 8, Rule 1 -- service out of Singapore with the Court's approval`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:639 | 1. —(1) An originating process or other court document may be served out of Singapore with the Court’s approval if it can be shown that the Court has
-- src:639 | the jurisdiction or is the appropriate court to hear the action.
@ref O 8 r 1(1) (src:639)
GIVEN `it can be shown that the Court has the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be shown that the Court is the appropriate court to hear the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 1(1) the document may be served out of Singapore with the Court's approval` MEANS
    IF `it can be shown that the Court has the jurisdiction` OR `it can be shown that the Court is the appropriate court to hear the action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it can be shown that the Court has the jurisdiction or is the appropriate court to hear the action" (a failed "if", marginal reading)

-- src:639-644 | (2) To obtain the Court’s approval, the claimant must apply to the Court by summons without notice and supported by affidavit which must state — ( a )
-- src:639-644 | why the Court has the jurisdiction or is the appropriate court to hear the action; ( b ) in which country or place the defendant is, or probably may
-- src:639-644 | be found; and ( c ) whether the validity of the originating process needs to be extended.
@ref O 8 r 1(2) (src:639-644)
GIVEN `the claimant is applying to obtain the Court's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 1(2) the claimant must apply to the Court by summons without notice, supported by affidavit` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is applying to obtain the Court's approval`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for a claimant who applies "To obtain the Court’s approval"

-- src:639-644 | (2) To obtain the Court’s approval, the claimant must apply to the Court by summons without notice and supported by affidavit which must state — ( a )
-- src:639-644 | why the Court has the jurisdiction or is the appropriate court to hear the action; ( b ) in which country or place the defendant is, or probably may
-- src:639-644 | be found; and ( c ) whether the validity of the originating process needs to be extended.
@ref O 8 r 1(2) (src:639-644)
GIVEN `the claimant is applying to obtain the Court's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant applies by summons without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is supported by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states why the Court has the jurisdiction or is the appropriate court to hear the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states in which country or place the defendant is, or probably may be found` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states whether the validity of the originating process needs to be extended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 1(2) the application for the Court's approval is made as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claimant is applying to obtain the Court's approval`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for a claimant who applies "To obtain the Court’s approval"
        IF `the claimant applies by summons without notice` AND `the application is supported by affidavit`
           AND `the affidavit states why the Court has the jurisdiction or is the appropriate court to hear the action`
           AND `the affidavit states in which country or place the defendant is, or probably may be found`
           AND `the affidavit states whether the validity of the originating process needs to be extended`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant must apply to the Court by summons without notice and supported by affidavit which must state" the three matters

-- src:645 | (3) The Court’s approval is not required if service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties.
@ref O 8 r 1(3) (src:645)
GIVEN `service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 1(3) the Court's approval is not required` MEANS
    IF `service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court’s approval is not required if service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties" (a failed "if", marginal reading)

-- src:646 | (4) The Court’s approval is not required for service of court documents other than the originating process if the Court’s approval has been granted
-- src:646 | for service of the originating process out of Singapore.
@ref O 8 r 1(4) (src:646)
GIVEN `the document is a court document other than the originating process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 1(4) the Court's approval is not required for service of the document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the document is a court document other than the originating process`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (4) reaches "court documents other than the originating process"
        IF `the Court's approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Court’s approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore" (a failed "if", marginal reading)

-- Gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B, guidance for hand-gathering only): paragraphs (3) and (4) are the two routes to "approval is not required".
-- They do not say they are the only two, so when neither holds the gathered answer is NOTHING.
-- src:645-646 | (3) The Court’s approval is not required if service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties. (4) The Court’s approval is not
-- src:645-646 | required for service of court documents other than the originating process if the Court’s approval has been granted for service of the originating
-- src:645-646 | process out of Singapore.
@ref O 8 r 1 (src:645-646)
GIVEN `service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a court document other than the originating process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 1 the Court's approval is not required to serve the document out of Singapore` MEANS
    IF (`o 8 r 1(3) the Court's approval is not required` `service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`o 8 r 1(4) the Court's approval is not required for service of the document` `the document is a court document other than the originating process` `the Court's approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (3) and (4) say when approval is not required and have no "only"

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 8, Rule 2 -- methods of service out of Singapore`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 8 r 2(1) the manner of service out of Singapore` IS ONE OF
    `o 8 r 2(1)(a) the manner contractually agreed between the parties`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(i)(A) Rule 4A or Rule 6, whichever is applicable`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(i)(B) a manner in sub-paragraph (a), (c), (d), (e) or (f), subject to any objection made by the receiving Contracting State`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(ii) the manner provided in the other Civil Procedure Convention`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(iii) either of the manners in sub-paragraph (i) or (ii)`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(c) through the government of the foreign country`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(d) through the judicial authority of the foreign country`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(e) through a Singapore consular authority in the foreign country`
    `o 8 r 2(1)(f) the manner provided by the law of the foreign country`
    `o 8 r 2(1) some other manner`

-- src:648-667 | 2. —(1) Where the Court’s approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2), service of the originating process or other court documents may be effected out
-- src:648-667 | of Singapore in the following manner: ( a ) according to the manner contractually agreed between the parties; ( b ) where there is a Civil Procedure
-- src:648-667 | Convention governing service in the foreign country — (i) in the case of the Hague Service Convention as defined in Rule 4A(7) — (A) in accordance
-- src:648-667 | with Rule 4A or 6, whichever is applicable; or (B) subject to any objection made by the receiving Contracting State, in accordance with sub-paragraph
-- src:648-667 | ( a ), ( c ), ( d ), ( e ) or ( f ); (ii) in the case of any other Civil Procedure Convention — according to the manner provided in that convention;
-- src:648-667 | or (iii) in the case where both the Hague Service Convention and another Civil Procedure Convention govern service in the foreign country — in
-- src:648-667 | accordance with either sub-paragraph (i) or (ii); [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023] ( c ) through the government of the foreign country if that government
-- src:648-667 | is willing to effect service; ( d ) through the judicial authority of the foreign country if that authority is willing to effect service; ( e )
-- src:648-667 | through a Singapore consular authority in the foreign country seeking the assistance of the relevant authority in that foreign country to effect
-- src:648-667 | service; [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023] ( f ) according to the manner provided by the law of that foreign country.
@ref O 8 r 2(1) (src:648-667)
GIVEN `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A `o 8 r 2(1) the manner of service out of Singapore`
      `the Hague Service Convention governs service in the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Civil Procedure Convention governs service in the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign government is willing to effect service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign judicial authority is willing to effect service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiving Contracting State has made an objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 2(1) service out of Singapore may be effected in that manner` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Court’s approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER manner
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(a) the manner contractually agreed between the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(i)(A) Rule 4A or Rule 6, whichever is applicable` THEN
            IF `the Hague Service Convention governs service in the foreign country`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is a Civil Procedure Convention governing service in the foreign country ... in the case of the Hague Service Convention"
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(i)(B) a manner in sub-paragraph (a), (c), (d), (e) or (f), subject to any objection made by the receiving Contracting State` THEN
            IF `the Hague Service Convention governs service in the foreign country`
            THEN
                IF `the receiving Contracting State has made an objection`
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any objection made by the receiving Contracting State" depends on what the State objected to, which is not in these Rules
                ELSE JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is a Civil Procedure Convention governing service in the foreign country ... in the case of the Hague Service Convention"
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(ii) the manner provided in the other Civil Procedure Convention` THEN
            IF `another Civil Procedure Convention governs service in the foreign country`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where there is a Civil Procedure Convention governing service in the foreign country ... in the case of any other Civil Procedure Convention"
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(b)(iii) either of the manners in sub-paragraph (i) or (ii)` THEN
            IF `the Hague Service Convention governs service in the foreign country` AND `another Civil Procedure Convention governs service in the foreign country`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case where both the Hague Service Convention and another Civil Procedure Convention govern service in the foreign country"
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(c) through the government of the foreign country` THEN
            IF `the foreign government is willing to effect service`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "through the government of the foreign country if that government is willing to effect service"
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(d) through the judicial authority of the foreign country` THEN
            IF `the foreign judicial authority is willing to effect service`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "through the judicial authority of the foreign country if that authority is willing to effect service"
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(e) through a Singapore consular authority in the foreign country` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1)(f) the manner provided by the law of the foreign country` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 8 r 2(1) some other manner` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be effected out of Singapore in the following manner" has no "only"

