-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 8, Rules 3 and 4 -- Malaysia and Brunei Darussalam; State Courts`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 8 r 3 how the originating process is served on the defendant` IS ONE OF
    `o 8 r 3(a) in accordance with Rule 2`
    `o 8 r 3(b) sent by post or otherwise by the Registrar to an appropriate officer of a court in the area`
    `o 8 r 3 some other manner`

-- src:674-677 | 3. Where the defendant is in Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam, the originating process — ( a ) may be served in accordance with Rule 2; or ( b ) may be
-- src:674-677 | sent by post or otherwise by the Registrar to the Magistrate, Registrar or other appropriate officer of any court exercising civil jurisdiction in the
-- src:674-677 | area in which the person to be served is said to be or to be carrying on business for service on the defendant, and if it is returned with an
-- src:674-677 | endorsement of service and with an affidavit of such service, it is deemed to have been duly served.
@ref O 8 r 3 (src:674-677)
GIVEN `the defendant is in Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A `o 8 r 3 how the originating process is served on the defendant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 3 the originating process may be served in that manner` MEANS
    IF NOT `the defendant is in Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the defendant is in Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER manner
        WHEN `o 8 r 3(a) in accordance with Rule 2` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 8 r 3(b) sent by post or otherwise by the Registrar to an appropriate officer of a court in the area` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 8 r 3 some other manner` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be served in accordance with Rule 2; or may be sent by post" has no "only"

-- src:677 | and if it is returned with an endorsement of service and with an affidavit of such service, it is deemed to have been duly served.
@ref O 8 r 3(b) (src:677)
GIVEN `the Registrar sent it to an appropriate officer of a court in the area for service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is returned with an endorsement of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is returned with an affidavit of such service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 3(b) the originating process is deemed to have been duly served` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Registrar sent it to an appropriate officer of a court in the area for service`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of an originating process sent under sub-paragraph (b)
        IF `it is returned with an endorsement of service` AND `it is returned with an affidavit of such service`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is returned with an endorsement of service and with an affidavit of such service, it is deemed to have been duly served" (a failed "if", marginal reading)

-- src:679-682 | 4. —(1) An originating process issued in the State Courts which is to be served out of Singapore in any jurisdiction (other than Malaysia or Brunei
-- src:679-682 | Darussalam) — ( a ) must be sent by the Registrar of the State Courts to the Registrar of the Supreme Court; and ( b ) must be served in accordance
-- src:679-682 | with these Rules relating to the service out of Singapore of an originating process issued in the Supreme Court.
@ref O 8 r 4(1) (src:679-682)
GIVEN `the originating process was issued in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurisdiction is Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4(1) the Registrar of the State Courts must send the originating process to the Registrar of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    IF `the originating process was issued in the State Courts` AND `it is to be served out of Singapore` AND (NOT `the jurisdiction is Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) reaches an originating process "issued in the State Courts which is to be served out of Singapore in any jurisdiction (other than Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam)"

-- src:679-682 | 4. —(1) An originating process issued in the State Courts which is to be served out of Singapore in any jurisdiction (other than Malaysia or Brunei
-- src:679-682 | Darussalam) — ( a ) must be sent by the Registrar of the State Courts to the Registrar of the Supreme Court; and ( b ) must be served in accordance
-- src:679-682 | with these Rules relating to the service out of Singapore of an originating process issued in the Supreme Court.
@ref O 8 r 4(1) (src:679-682)
GIVEN `the originating process was issued in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurisdiction is Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar of the State Courts has sent it to the Registrar of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4(1)(a) it has been sent by the Registrar of the State Courts to the Registrar of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the originating process was issued in the State Courts`) OR (NOT `it is to be served out of Singapore`) OR `the jurisdiction is Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) reaches an originating process "issued in the State Courts which is to be served out of Singapore in any jurisdiction (other than Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam)"
        IF `the Registrar of the State Courts has sent it to the Registrar of the Supreme Court`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be sent by the Registrar of the State Courts to the Registrar of the Supreme Court"

-- src:679-682 | 4. —(1) An originating process issued in the State Courts which is to be served out of Singapore in any jurisdiction (other than Malaysia or Brunei
-- src:679-682 | Darussalam) — ( a ) must be sent by the Registrar of the State Courts to the Registrar of the Supreme Court; and ( b ) must be served in accordance
-- src:679-682 | with these Rules relating to the service out of Singapore of an originating process issued in the Supreme Court.
@ref O 8 r 4(1) (src:679-682)
GIVEN `the originating process was issued in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurisdiction is Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served in accordance with these Rules relating to the service out of Singapore of an originating process issued in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4(1)(b) it has been served in accordance with the Rules for an originating process issued in the Supreme Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the originating process was issued in the State Courts`) OR (NOT `it is to be served out of Singapore`) OR `the jurisdiction is Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) reaches an originating process "issued in the State Courts which is to be served out of Singapore in any jurisdiction (other than Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam)"
        IF `it is served in accordance with these Rules relating to the service out of Singapore of an originating process issued in the Supreme Court`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be served in accordance with these Rules relating to the service out of Singapore of an originating process issued in the Supreme Court"

-- src:683 | (2) Every certificate of service received by the Registrar of the Supreme Court in respect of such service must be transmitted by the Registrar of the
-- src:683 | Supreme Court to the Registrar of the State Courts.
@ref O 8 r 4(2) (src:683)
GIVEN `a certificate of service has been received by the Registrar of the Supreme Court in respect of such service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4(2) the Registrar of the Supreme Court must transmit the certificate to the Registrar of the State Courts` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of service has been received by the Registrar of the Supreme Court in respect of such service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "Every certificate of service received ... in respect of such service"

-- src:683 | (2) Every certificate of service received by the Registrar of the Supreme Court in respect of such service must be transmitted by the Registrar of the
-- src:683 | Supreme Court to the Registrar of the State Courts.
@ref O 8 r 4(2) (src:683)
GIVEN `a certificate of service has been received by the Registrar of the Supreme Court in respect of such service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar of the Supreme Court has transmitted it to the Registrar of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4(2) the certificate has been transmitted as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a certificate of service has been received by the Registrar of the Supreme Court in respect of such service`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "Every certificate of service received ... in respect of such service"
        IF `the Registrar of the Supreme Court has transmitted it to the Registrar of the State Courts`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be transmitted by the Registrar of the Supreme Court to the Registrar of the State Courts"

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 8, Rule 4A -- the Hague Service Convention`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:685 | 4A. —(1) This Rule applies to the service out of Singapore, under Article 3 of the Hague Service Convention, of an originating process or other court
-- src:685 | document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter on a person, other than a State, in a Contracting
-- src:685 | State.
@ref O 8 r 4A(1) (src:685)
GIVEN `the service is under Article 3 of the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is an originating process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be served is a State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be served is in a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(1) this Rule applies to the service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person to be served is a State`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on a person, other than a State, in a Contracting State"
        IF `the service is under Article 3 of the Hague Service Convention`
           AND `the document is an originating process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter`
           AND `the person to be served is in a Contracting State`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Rule applies to the service out of Singapore, under Article 3 of the Hague Service Convention" of such a document on a person in a Contracting State, with no "only"

-- src:685 | (2) If any provision in this Rule is inconsistent with any other provision in this Order, the provision in this Rule prevails to the extent of the
-- src:685 | inconsistency.
@ref O 8 r 4A(2) (src:685)
GIVEN `the provision in this Rule is inconsistent with another provision in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(2) the provision in Rule 4A prevails over the other provision in this Order` MEANS
    IF `the provision in this Rule is inconsistent with another provision in this Order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any provision in this Rule is inconsistent with any other provision in this Order" (a failed "if", marginal reading)

-- src:686 | (3) The person mentioned in paragraph (1) must have a known address in the Contracting State in which the documents are to be served.
@ref O 8 r 4A(3) (src:686)
GIVEN `the person is the person mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a known address in the Contracting State in which the documents are to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(3) the person has a known address as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is the person mentioned in paragraph (1)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is of "The person mentioned in paragraph (1)"
        IF `the person has a known address in the Contracting State in which the documents are to be served`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have a known address in the Contracting State in which the documents are to be served"

-- src:687-694 | (4) A person who wishes to serve any document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule must file in the Registry a request for
-- src:687-694 | service in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form, accompanied by — ( a ) a sealed copy of the document to be served; ( b ) a summary of the
-- src:687-694 | document to be served, in accordance with Part 3 of the Model Form; ( c ) a translation of the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs ( a ) and ( b )
-- src:687-694 | in accordance with Rule 2(4) and (5); and ( d ) a copy each of the request and the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs ( a ), ( b ) and ( c ), which
-- src:687-694 | may be in electronic form if agreed to by the central authority.
@ref O 8 r 4A(4) (src:687-694)
GIVEN `the person wishes to serve a document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(4) the person must file in the Registry a request for service in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form` MEANS
    IF `the person wishes to serve a document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "A person who wishes to serve any document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule"

-- Sub-paragraph (c) takes the answers of Rule 2(4) and Rule 2(5) as inputs, because it is "in accordance with Rule 2(4) and (5)".
-- src:687-694 | (4) A person who wishes to serve any document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule must file in the Registry a request for
-- src:687-694 | service in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form, accompanied by — ( a ) a sealed copy of the document to be served; ( b ) a summary of the
-- src:687-694 | document to be served, in accordance with Part 3 of the Model Form; ( c ) a translation of the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs ( a ) and ( b )
-- src:687-694 | in accordance with Rule 2(4) and (5); and ( d ) a copy each of the request and the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs ( a ), ( b ) and ( c ), which
-- src:687-694 | may be in electronic form if agreed to by the central authority.
@ref O 8 r 4A(4) (src:687-694)
GIVEN `the person wishes to serve a document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is filed in the Registry in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sealed copy of the document to be served accompanies the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a summary of the document to be served in accordance with Part 3 of the Model Form accompanies the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the translation of the documents in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) is accompanying as Rule 2(4) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the translation of the documents in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) is certified as Rule 2(5) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a copy each of the request and the documents in sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) accompanies the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(4) the request has been filed with the documents the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person wishes to serve a document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "A person who wishes to serve any document mentioned in paragraph (1) out of Singapore under this Rule"
        IF (NOT `the request is filed in the Registry in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form`)
           OR (NOT `a sealed copy of the document to be served accompanies the request`)
           OR (NOT `a summary of the document to be served in accordance with Part 3 of the Model Form accompanies the request`)
           OR (NOT `a copy each of the request and the documents in sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) accompanies the request`)
           OR `the translation of the documents in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) is accompanying as Rule 2(4) requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           OR `the translation of the documents in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) is certified as Rule 2(5) requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must file in the Registry a request for service in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form, accompanied by" the four things
        IF `the translation of the documents in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) is accompanying as Rule 2(4) requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the translation of the documents in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) is certified as Rule 2(5) requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the translation meets Rule 2(4) and (5) is not decided on these facts

-- src:694 | a copy each of the request and the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs ( a ), ( b ) and ( c ), which may be in electronic form if agreed to by the
-- src:694 | central authority.
@ref O 8 r 4A(4)(d) (src:694)
GIVEN `the central authority has agreed to electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(4)(d) the copies may be in electronic form` MEANS
    IF `the central authority has agreed to electronic form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which may be in electronic form if agreed to by the central authority" (a failed "if", marginal reading)

-- src:695 | (5) The Registrar must send the documents filed under paragraph (4) to the central authority of the Contracting State in which the documents are to be
-- src:695 | served.
@ref O 8 r 4A(5) (src:695)
GIVEN `documents have been filed under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(5) the Registrar must send the documents to the central authority` MEANS
    IF `documents have been filed under paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "the documents filed under paragraph (4)"

-- src:695 | (5) The Registrar must send the documents filed under paragraph (4) to the central authority of the Contracting State in which the documents are to be
-- src:695 | served.
@ref O 8 r 4A(5) (src:695)
GIVEN `documents have been filed under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has sent the documents to the central authority of the Contracting State in which the documents are to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(5) the Registrar has sent the documents as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `documents have been filed under paragraph (4)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "the documents filed under paragraph (4)"
        IF `the Registrar has sent the documents to the central authority of the Contracting State in which the documents are to be served`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must send the documents filed under paragraph (4) to the central authority of the Contracting State in which the documents are to be served"

-- src:696 | (6) Rule 2(3) does not apply in relation to any service under this Rule.
@ref O 8 r 4A(6) (src:696)
GIVEN `the service is under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(6) Rule 2(3) applies to the service` MEANS
    IF `the service is under this Rule`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rule 2(3) does not apply in relation to any service under this Rule"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches "any service under this Rule" only

-- src:697 | (7) In this Rule — “central authority”, in relation to a Contracting State, means an authority that is designated by that State under Article 2 of the
-- src:697 | Hague Service Convention for receiving requests for service coming from other State parties to the Hague Service Convention;
@ref O 8 r 4A(7) “central authority” (src:697)
GIVEN `it is an authority designated by the Contracting State under Article 2 of the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designated for receiving requests for service coming from other State parties to the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(7) an authority is a central authority` MEANS
    IF `it is an authority designated by the Contracting State under Article 2 of the Hague Service Convention` AND `it is designated for receiving requests for service coming from other State parties to the Hague Service Convention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“central authority” ... means an authority that is designated by that State under Article 2 of the Hague Service Convention for receiving requests for service coming from other State parties to the Hague Service Convention"

-- src:698 | “Contracting State” means a State (other than Singapore) which is a party to the Hague Service Convention;
@ref O 8 r 4A(7) “Contracting State” (src:698)
GIVEN `it is a State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a party to the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(7) a State is a Contracting State` MEANS
    IF `it is a State` AND (NOT `it is Singapore`) AND `it is a party to the Hague Service Convention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Contracting State” means a State (other than Singapore) which is a party to the Hague Service Convention"

-- src:699 | “Hague Service Convention” means the Convention on the Service Abroad of Judicial and Extrajudicial Documents in Civil or Commercial Matters done at
-- src:699 | The Hague on 15 November 1965;
@ref O 8 r 4A(7) “Hague Service Convention” (src:699)
GIVEN `it is the Convention on the Service Abroad of Judicial and Extrajudicial Documents in Civil or Commercial Matters done at The Hague on 15 November 1965` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(7) an instrument is the Hague Service Convention` MEANS
    IF `it is the Convention on the Service Abroad of Judicial and Extrajudicial Documents in Civil or Commercial Matters done at The Hague on 15 November 1965`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Hague Service Convention” means the Convention on the Service Abroad of Judicial and Extrajudicial Documents in Civil or Commercial Matters done at The Hague on 15 November 1965"

-- src:700 | “Model Form” means the model form, in 3 parts, annexed to the Hague Service Convention and set out on the Internet website for that Convention at
-- src:700 | https://www.hcch.net/en/​instruments/conventions/specialised-sections/service
@ref O 8 r 4A(7) “Model Form” (src:700)
GIVEN `it is the model form, in 3 parts, annexed to the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is set out on the Internet website for that Convention at the address the Rule gives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 4A(7) a form is the Model Form` MEANS
    IF `it is the model form, in 3 parts, annexed to the Hague Service Convention` AND `it is set out on the Internet website for that Convention at the address the Rule gives`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Model Form” means the model form, in 3 parts, annexed to the Hague Service Convention and set out on the Internet website for that Convention"

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 8, Rules 5 and 6 -- the Warsaw Convention; a foreign State`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:702-707 | 5. —(1) Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2), a person who wishes to serve an originating process on a High Contracting Party to the
-- src:702-707 | Warsaw Convention to enforce a claim in respect of carriage undertaken by that Party, must file in the Registry — ( a ) a request for the Ministry of
-- src:702-707 | Foreign Affairs to arrange service; ( b ) a sealed copy of the originating process; and ( c ) a translation of the originating process in the official
-- src:702-707 | language of the High Contracting Party or, if there is more than one official language, in any of those languages which is appropriate for the High
-- src:702-707 | Contracting Party to be served, except where the official language or one of the official languages is English.
@ref O 8 r 5(1) (src:702-707)
GIVEN `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a High Contracting Party to the Warsaw Convention to enforce a claim in respect of carriage undertaken by that Party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 5(1) the person must file in the Registry the request, the sealed copy and the translation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a High Contracting Party to the Warsaw Convention to enforce a claim in respect of carriage undertaken by that Party`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "a person who wishes to serve an originating process on a High Contracting Party to the Warsaw Convention to enforce a claim in respect of carriage undertaken by that Party"
        IF NOT `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2)" ("upon" counts as "where")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:702-707 | 5. —(1) Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2), a person who wishes to serve an originating process on a High Contracting Party to the
-- src:702-707 | Warsaw Convention to enforce a claim in respect of carriage undertaken by that Party, must file in the Registry — ( a ) a request for the Ministry of
-- src:702-707 | Foreign Affairs to arrange service; ( b ) a sealed copy of the originating process; and ( c ) a translation of the originating process in the official
-- src:702-707 | language of the High Contracting Party or, if there is more than one official language, in any of those languages which is appropriate for the High
-- src:702-707 | Contracting Party to be served, except where the official language or one of the official languages is English.
@ref O 8 r 5(1) (src:702-707)
GIVEN `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a High Contracting Party to the Warsaw Convention to enforce a claim in respect of carriage undertaken by that Party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sealed copy of the originating process is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a translation of the originating process in the official language, or an appropriate one of several, is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official language or one of the official languages is English` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 5(1) the person has filed in the Registry what the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a High Contracting Party to the Warsaw Convention to enforce a claim in respect of carriage undertaken by that Party`) OR (NOT `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of a person who wishes to serve on a High Contracting Party, "Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2)"
        IF `a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service is filed` AND `a sealed copy of the originating process is filed`
           AND (`a translation of the originating process in the official language, or an appropriate one of several, is filed` OR `the official language or one of the official languages is English`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must file in the Registry (a) a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service; (b) a sealed copy of the originating process; and (c) a translation of the originating process ... except where the official language or one of the official languages is English"

-- src:708 | (2) Every translation filed under paragraph (1)( c ) must be certified by a person qualified to do so and the certificate must contain the
-- src:708 | translator’s full name, his or her address and his or her qualifications.
@ref O 8 r 5(2) (src:708)
GIVEN `it is a translation filed under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is certified by a person qualified to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains the translator's full name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains the translator's address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains the translator's qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 5(2) the translation is certified as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a translation filed under paragraph (1)(c)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "Every translation filed under paragraph (1)( c )"
        IF `it is certified by a person qualified to do so` AND `the certificate contains the translator's full name` AND `the certificate contains the translator's address` AND `the certificate contains the translator's qualifications`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be certified by a person qualified to do so and the certificate must contain the translator’s full name, his or her address and his or her qualifications"

-- src:709 | (3) The serving party must engage a solicitor for the purposes of filing the necessary documents under paragraph (1).
@ref O 8 r 5(3) (src:709)
