`o 8 r 5(3) the serving party has engaged a solicitor as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `documents are to be filed under paragraph (1)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "for the purposes of filing the necessary documents under paragraph (1)"
        IF `the serving party has engaged a solicitor`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The serving party must engage a solicitor for the purposes of filing the necessary documents under paragraph (1)"

-- src:710 | (4) The Registrar must send the documents filed under paragraph (1) to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for the originating process to be served on the
-- src:710 | High Contracting Party or the government in question.
@ref O 8 r 5(4) (src:710)
GIVEN `documents have been filed under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 5(4) the Registrar must send the documents to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs` MEANS
    IF `documents have been filed under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "the documents filed under paragraph (1)"

-- src:710 | (4) The Registrar must send the documents filed under paragraph (1) to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for the originating process to be served on the
-- src:710 | High Contracting Party or the government in question.
@ref O 8 r 5(4) (src:710)
GIVEN `documents have been filed under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has sent the documents to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 5(4) the Registrar has sent the documents as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `documents have been filed under paragraph (1)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "the documents filed under paragraph (1)"
        IF `the Registrar has sent the documents to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must send the documents filed under paragraph (1) to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs"

-- src:712-717 | 6. —(1) Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2), a person who wishes to serve an originating process on a State, as defined in section 16
-- src:712-717 | of the State Immunity Act, must file in the Registry — ( a ) a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service; ( b ) a sealed copy of
-- src:712-717 | the originating process; and ( c ) a translation of the originating process in the official language of the State or, if there is more than one
-- src:712-717 | official language, in any of those languages which is appropriate for the State to be served, except where the official language or one of the
-- src:712-717 | official languages is English.
@ref O 8 r 6(1) (src:712-717)
GIVEN `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a State, as defined in section 16 of the State Immunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 6(1) the person must file in the Registry the request, the sealed copy and the translation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a State, as defined in section 16 of the State Immunity Act`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "a person who wishes to serve an originating process on a State, as defined in section 16 of the State Immunity Act"
        IF NOT `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2)" ("upon" counts as "where")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:712-717 | 6. —(1) Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2), a person who wishes to serve an originating process on a State, as defined in section 16
-- src:712-717 | of the State Immunity Act, must file in the Registry — ( a ) a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service; ( b ) a sealed copy of
-- src:712-717 | the originating process; and ( c ) a translation of the originating process in the official language of the State or, if there is more than one
-- src:712-717 | official language, in any of those languages which is appropriate for the State to be served, except where the official language or one of the
-- src:712-717 | official languages is English.
@ref O 8 r 6(1) (src:712-717)
GIVEN `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a State, as defined in section 16 of the State Immunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sealed copy of the originating process is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a translation of the originating process in the official language, or an appropriate one of several, is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official language or one of the official languages is English` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 6(1) the person has filed in the Registry what the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person wishes to serve an originating process on a State, as defined in section 16 of the State Immunity Act`) OR (NOT `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of a person who wishes to serve on a State, "Upon obtaining the Court’s approval under Rule 1(2)"
        IF `a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service is filed` AND `a sealed copy of the originating process is filed`
           AND (`a translation of the originating process in the official language, or an appropriate one of several, is filed` OR `the official language or one of the official languages is English`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must file in the Registry (a) a request for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to arrange service; (b) a sealed copy of the originating process; and (c) a translation of the originating process ... except where the official language or one of the official languages is English"

-- src:718 | (2) Every translation filed under paragraph (1)( c ) must be certified by a person qualified to do so and the certificate must contain the
-- src:718 | translator’s full name, his or her address and his or her qualifications.
@ref O 8 r 6(2) (src:718)
GIVEN `it is a translation filed under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is certified by a person qualified to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains the translator's full name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains the translator's address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate contains the translator's qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 6(2) the translation is certified as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a translation filed under paragraph (1)(c)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "Every translation filed under paragraph (1)( c )"
        IF `it is certified by a person qualified to do so` AND `the certificate contains the translator's full name` AND `the certificate contains the translator's address` AND `the certificate contains the translator's qualifications`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be certified by a person qualified to do so and the certificate must contain the translator’s full name, his or her address and his or her qualifications"

