DECLARE `o 8 r 6(5) the method of serving the originating process on the State` IS ONE OF
    `o 8 r 6(5) the method agreed`
    `o 8 r 6(5) in accordance with this Rule`
    `o 8 r 6(5) some other method`

-- src:721 | (5) Where section 14(6) of the State Immunity Act applies and the State has agreed to a method of service other than that provided by this Rule, the
-- src:721 | originating process may be served either by the method agreed or in accordance with this Rule.
@ref O 8 r 6(5) (src:721)
GIVEN `section 14(6) of the State Immunity Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State has agreed to a method of service other than that provided by this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      method IS A `o 8 r 6(5) the method of serving the originating process on the State`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 6(5) the originating process may be served by that method` MEANS
    IF NOT (`section 14(6) of the State Immunity Act applies` AND `the State has agreed to a method of service other than that provided by this Rule`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where section 14(6) of the State Immunity Act applies and the State has agreed to a method of service other than that provided by this Rule"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER method
        WHEN `o 8 r 6(5) the method agreed` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 8 r 6(5) in accordance with this Rule` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 8 r 6(5) some other method` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be served either by the method agreed or in accordance with this Rule" has no "only"

