    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon request to pay the expenses" ("upon" counts as "where")

-- src:727 | 8. An official certificate or letter by the agency or person who effected service in the foreign country stating that service has been effected on the
-- src:727 | party to be served in accordance with the law of the foreign country and the date of the service is evidence of those facts.
@ref O 8 r 8 (src:727)
GIVEN `it is an official certificate or letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by the agency or person who effected service in the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that service has been effected on the party to be served in accordance with the law of the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the date of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 8 r 8 the certificate or letter is evidence of the service and its date` MEANS
    IF `it is an official certificate or letter` AND `it is by the agency or person who effected service in the foreign country` AND `it states that service has been effected on the party to be served in accordance with the law of the foreign country` AND `it states the date of the service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is evidence of those facts" says what such a certificate or letter proves and does not say that no other document does
